<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palace of Westminster</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Houses of Parliament</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Palace of Westminster in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> is the meeting place of the Parliament of the United Kingdom, and before it of the Parliaments of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>. A royal palace from the 11th century, it was rebuilt in Gothic Revival style by Charles Barry and Augustus Pugin after a fire in 1834, and the name Westminster is used for Parliament itself.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palace-of-westminster.jpg" alt="Palace of Westminster" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ThatsTheBoss · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palace_of_Westminster_as_seen_from_Westminster_Bridge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
